\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. It came upon the midnight clear,
\par That glorious song of old,
\par From angels bending near the earth
\par To touch their harps of gold:
\par Peace on  the earth, good-will to them,
\par From heaven's all-gracious King!
\par The world in solemn stillness lay
\par To hear the angels sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Still through the cloven skies they come
\par With peaceful wings unfurled;
\par And still their heavenly music floats
\par O'er all the weary world;
\par Above its sad and lowly plains
\par They bend on hovering wing,
\par And ever o'er its Babel sounds
\par The blessed angels sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But with the woes of sin and strife
\par The world has suffered long;
\par Beneath the angel strain have rolled
\par Two thousand years of wrong;
\par And man, at war with man, hears not
\par The love song which they bring:
\par O hush the noise, ye man of strife,
\par And hear the angels sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And ye, beneath life's crushing load
\par Whose forms are bending low,
\par Who toil along the climbing way
\par With painful steps and slow-
\par Look now! for glad and golden hours
\par Come swiftly on the wing:
\par O rest beside the weary road,
\par And hear the angels sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For lo! the days are hastening on,
\par By prophet bards foretold,
\par When with the ever-circling years
\par Comes round the age of gold.
\par When peace shall over all the earth
\par Its ancient splendours fling,
\par And the whole world give back the song
\par Which now  the angels sing.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

